    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2PGHTAG7Ju4Mw8ZC3zoPzju)_\n\nBefore: discourse-graphs could tell me a claim was contested only through its own dashboards, its status logic was fixed, and the research-question states I had sketched had one catch-all `CONTESTED` state.\n\nAfter: a new `sp-dg-positions` module draws the positions in a discourse graph the way `sp-vulpea-hierarchy` draws the note hierarchy, with the same kind of interface (`dg-positions-outline`, `dg-positions-graph`, `dg-positions-rankdir`, `dg-positions-graph-file`). It adds one view per status (`dg-positions-status`), a gaps view and a check view. Questions, claims, evidence and sources, the relations between them, the statuses and the gaps are all declared in one readable list, `dg-positions-rules`, so a new relation such as `contests` or `reframes` is one line. A new doc, `docs/tangles/research-question-states.org`, says exactly which state each object should be in; how contested an answer is now lives on the answer, not on the question.\n\nHow: the module reads `dg-all-nodes` and `dg-all-relations` from the discourse-graphs database and never writes to a note. `dg-positions-install` copies the declared node types and relations into discourse-graphs' own variables so it parses the new `DG_<RELATION>` properties; run `dg-rebuild-cache` afterwards. The literate doc `docs/tangles/custom/sp-dg-positions.org` is the source and tangles to `libraries/modules/custom/sp-dg-positions.el`; it is loaded from `init.el` after `sp-vulpea-hierarchy`. The doc's nine ERT tests pass in Emacs batch mode, the file byte-compiles without warnings, and the graph was rendered with Graphviz. It has not been run against a real discourse-graphs database.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01KPtqz2rJ4M5MmMAbr8fu1U)_",
